<title>UK: Tesco names Terry Leahy CEO.</title>
<headline>Tesco names Terry Leahy CEO.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>British supermarket chain Tesco Plc said on Friday that Terry Leahy had taken over as chief executive, filling the post previously held by its chairman, Lord MacLaurin.  </p>
<p>The company also said David Malpas, managing director, retired after almost 30 years with Tesco.</p>
<p>Lord MacLaurin will retire from the board at the company's annual general meeting in June.</p>
<p>John Gardiner, currently a non-executive deputy chairman of the company, will then become chairman on a part-time basis.</p>
<p>David Reid is currently deputy chairman.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
